.SH "NAME"
makeann \- prepare audio prompts for playback by rtpproxy
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.HP \w'\fBmakeann\fR\ 'u
\fBmakeann\fR [\fB\-l\fR\ \fIlimit\fR\ [\fB\-L\fR]] \fIinfile\fR [\fIoutfile_template\fR]
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.PP
\fBmakeann\fR
encodes an audio prompt into every codec that
\fBrtpproxy\fR(8)
can play it out in, using the
\fBP\fR
(play) command\&.
.PP
\fIinfile\fR
has to contain raw signed 16\-bit little\-endian mono samples at 8 kHz, with no header\&. Such a file can be produced, for example, with
\fBsox\fR:
.sp
.if n \{\
.RS 4
.\}
.nf
sox prompt\&.wav \-t raw \-r 8000 \-c 1 \-b 16 \-e signed\-integer \e
    \-L prompt\&.sln
.fi
.if n \{\
.RE
.\}
.PP
For each codec, the encoded prompt is written into a file named
\fIoutfile_template\fR\&.\fIpt\fR, where
\fIpt\fR
is the RTP payload type of the codec\&. If
\fIoutfile_template\fR
is not given,
\fIinfile\fR
is used instead\&. The following files are produced:
.PP
\fIoutfile_template\fR\&.0
.RS 4
G\&.711 u\-law\&.
.RE
.PP
\fIoutfile_template\fR\&.3
.RS 4
GSM 06\&.10, if GSM support has been compiled in\&.
.RE
.PP
\fIoutfile_template\fR\&.8
.RS 4
G\&.711 A\-law\&.
.RE
.PP
\fIoutfile_template\fR\&.9
.RS 4
G\&.722 at 64 kbit/s, if G\&.722 support has been compiled in\&.
.RE
.PP
\fIoutfile_template\fR\&.18
.RS 4
G\&.729, if G\&.729 support has been compiled in\&.
.RE
.PP
To play the prompt, give
\fIoutfile_template\fR
as the prompt name to the rtpproxy
\fBP\fR
command\&. rtpproxy tries the payload types listed in the command (or those of the session, if
session
is given instead) in order and plays the first one for which the file exists\&. Since rtpproxy changes its working directory to
/
when it daemonizes (unless started with
\fB\-D\fR), the prompt name should normally be an absolute path\&.
.SH "OPTIONS"
.PP
\fB\-l\fR \fIlimit\fR
.RS 4
Encode at most
\fIlimit\fR
samples (8000 samples per second) of the input\&.
.RE
.PP
\fB\-L\fR
.RS 4
Loop mode: repeat the input as many times as needed to produce exactly
\fIlimit\fR
samples of output\&. Requires
\fB\-l\fR\&.
.RE
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
.PP
\fBmakeann\fR
exits 0 on success, and 1 if an error occurs\&.
.SH "EXAMPLES"
.PP
Prepare
ringback\&.sln
for playback as
ringback, producing
ringback\&.0,
ringback\&.8
and so on:
.sp
.if n \{\
.RS 4
.\}
.nf
makeann ringback\&.sln ringback
.fi
.if n \{\
.RE
.\}
.PP
Make a 30 seconds long prompt out of a shorter one:
.sp
.if n \{\
.RS 4
.\}
.nf
makeann \-l 240000 \-L beep\&.sln beep30
.fi
.if n \{\
.RE
.\}
